# Delivery loop

The master copy is `conduct/methodology/SKILL.md`, versioned by git tags. Clients pin a tag and add overlays. Code conduct is `conduct/conduct/SKILL.md`. Do not copy it.

The engine is the only status writer. Workers do not call the tracker.

Sweep reads `status.intake` (default Todo). One runner holds the ticket with a `DELIVERY_LEASE` comment. Ground, then build, then one pull request per land repo. Quality must be green. The merge is a squash. Trunk quality must be green before `dev.promote` and before the dev status. `dev.promote` runs only for repos listed in `dev.promote.repos`. Ship is a separate command unless `ship.afterDev` is set. A failed ship step leaves the dev status.

A required step that returned no has one heal: edit, wait, or login. There is no list of failure phrases. edit changes the owner of the failure. When that owner is this package, open branch `engine-heal/<ticket>`, label it `engine-heal`, and include the next patch after the highest `v*` tag. Do not push a commit to main. The `pull_request` `quality` check gates it. The workflow does not push a commit. It squash-merges only when the pull request has that branch and the `engine-heal` label, every changed file is on the auto-merge allowlist: `src/connectors` source, or a version-only package.json and package-lock.json. `src/engine`, `src/adapters`, `src/schema`, `src/bots`, and any other path need a normal review, and the green run is a GitHub Actions `pull_request` run of `.github/workflows/quality.yml` on that exact head whose file matches `main`. Anything else, including an unknown proof, gets a comment and a normal review. The workflow does not merge or tag it. Clients install the tag.

Heal caps live in `delivery-loop.yaml` under `heal.maxAttempts` and `heal.caps`. The default is 3 per failure type (`quality-red`, `merge-conflict`, `promote-failed`, `ship-failed`, `quality-pending`, `quality-unscheduled`, `runner-blocked`, `other`). The count is `OWNER_HEAL` comments on the ticket. At the cap the engine labels `heal-exhausted` and the failure type, writes `HEAL_EXHAUSTED`, and stops. A failed marker comment fails the heal.
